<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Bourbon-Condé</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Condé family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Bourbon-Condé was a branch of the French royal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a>, founded by Louis I de Bourbon, Prince of Condé, a Protestant leader in the Wars of Religion who died in 1569. Its members held the title of Prince of Condé and were among the greatest nobles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>; the most famous was Louis II, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-grand-conde">Great Condé</a>, a celebrated general. The line ended in 1830.</p></div>
